text:
marisa: heads-up — running into a nasty dual-publish + edge bootstrapping quirk in the sample app. Local Node (esm/cjs) works but the Next.js Edge function throws `TypeError: default is not a constructor` when importing our SDK in an edge runtime.

aj: ugh that sounds like an exports resolution mismatch. do you have your package.json exports + type fields handy?

marisa: yep, minimal excerpt:```json
"exports": {
  ".": {
    "import": "./dist/esm/index.js",
    "require": "./dist/cjs/index.js",
    "types": "./dist/types/index.d.ts"
  }
}```
next config is default; the error surfaces only when deployed to an edge runtime (Vercel Edge / Node edge env).

nora: two quick suspects: 1) bundler/edge runner treating package as CJS because of `main` or `types` placement, 2) dynamic default export interop differences between ESM->CJS. did you ship a separate `./edge` entry for ESM-only usage?

marisa: we don't. we tried forcing `type: "module"` but that broke a bunch of server-side CJS consumers (internal sample apps that still `require`).

li: Re: typing entrypoints — `types` is not part of conditional exports so some TS setups fallback to main. also bundlers sometimes prefer `require` when `main` exists. check that `main` is absent or points to CJS explicitly. if you need both, conditional exports should include an `edge` target.

aj: pattern we've used in other repos: add conditional export for edge/worker first, e.g.```json
"exports": {
  "./edge": { "import": "./dist/esm/edge.js" },
  ".": { "import": "./dist/esm/index.js", "require": "./dist/cjs/index.js" }
}```
then consumers in edge runtimes can `import { createClient } from 'sdk/edge'` (or you can let bundler alias it).

tom: +1. Another option: publish an `sdk-edge` package that's ESM-only. it's heavier operationally but avoids conditional export footguns.

marisa: the bigger surprise: auth/retry behaviour changes in edge — requests that should be retried once are retried twice and the body becomes empty on second attempt. suspect mismatch in our fetch polyfill or how we clone streams in edge env. not sure if this is related to packaging though.

nora: that sounds like the classic ReadableStream clone issue in workers. If you use `fetch`-style retry, you must either buffer the body (ArrayBuffer) or use `request.clone()` semantics that work in the environment. Edge runtimes sometimes don't support cloning the same way Node does.

li: can you paste the retry helper? Even tiny differences (using `node-fetch` vs native `fetch`) change the behavior. In edge we should rely on native `fetch` and do a body-buffer fallback for retries.

marisa: snippet:```js
async function retryFetch(input, init) {
  for (let i=0;i<2;i++) {
    const res = await fetch(input, init);
    if (res.ok) return res;
  }
  throw new Error('failed');
}
```
we pass `init.body` as a ReadableStream in some callers. second attempt fails because body is drained.

aj: yep. either buffer `init.body = await toArrayBuffer(body)` or make the SDK accept a factory `() => createRequest()` so callers can recreate the body per attempt. Document this in the SDK dx notes.

marisa: sounds good. For the packaging side, I'm leaning to: add a `./edge` conditional export (ESM-only), update README to recommend `import from 'sdk/edge'` for edge runtimes, and ship a tiny shim to normalize fetch cloning (edge-friendly).

devx-bot: created issue #4321: "edge: add edge export + retry body buffering" assigned to @marisa.

ops-bot: FYI deploy preview failed on the sample app earlier: https://vercel.com/preview/123 — logs show `TypeError: default is not a constructor` at /var/worker/edge-runtime.js:45.

nora: one more typing nit: ensure you include `types` inside exports for subpaths if you add `./edge`, e.g. `"./edge": { "types": "./dist/types/edge.d.ts", "import": "./dist/esm/edge.js" }` — otherwise TS auto-resolution might pick wrong declarations.

li: and add a tiny sample app in the repo `examples/edge` that imports the `./edge` entry; that'll be our repro for docs and CI smoke.

marisa: great, i'll prototype the conditional export + edge build and add buffering fallback for retries. i'll push a small repro to `examples/edge` and link it in the issue. thanks all. :thumbsup:

aj: thanks — ping us when the PR is up and we'll run the sample on Vercel/Next edge.

marisa: will do.
